From 4471760020e2efd281366734cd6598ac18f8beb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:45:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] bench: close the SAMPLE_LOG file

The r1 log opened from SAMPLE_LOG was never closed. Returning from main
flushes it anyway, but the handle leaked for the whole run and a caller
that reuses the code (or a sanitizer build) would see it; close it with
the other cleanup at the end of main.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GSaYLGdzq6d82nBLeSZFgB
---
 src/c/bench.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/c/bench.c b/src/c/bench.c
index 0a04077..a9cf3ca 100644
--- a/src/c/bench.c
+++ b/src/c/bench.c
@@ -263,5 +263,7 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
       printf("%d of %d instances FAILED\n", failures, ran);
   }
   free(r1_list);
+  if (opts.r1_log)
+    fclose(opts.r1_log);
   return failures ? 1 : 0;
 }
